WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Thursday,

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.173
the fifth of November. This
episode is written with AI,

3
00:00:07.227 --> 00:00:09.760
and read by an AI clone of my voice.

4
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.480
Crude fell about nine
percent on Wednesday.

5
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.560
The White House tied its
midterm losses to the Iran war,

6
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.387
and President Trump said he had
no immediate plans to strike Iran.

7
00:00:19.493 --> 00:00:22.880
Gas stayed tight, though, after a
fire took a Norwegian export field

8
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:23.960
offline.

9
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.160
On the markets. Brent lost eight dollars
ninety by early Wednesday afternoon

10
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.000
in New York. That left it at
ninety-four dollars seventy a barrel,

11
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.360
its lowest since the fourth of September.

12
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.693
West Texas Intermediate
fell eight dollars,

13
00:00:36.747 --> 00:00:38.520
to eighty-eight dollars ten.

14
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.060
Let's start with oil, and how
far the market moved in a week.

15
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.413
Brent was trading near one hundred
and eighteen dollars last Friday,

16
00:00:45.547 --> 00:00:47.360
according to OilPrice dot com.

17
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.360
Wednesday itself was volatile.

18
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.720
Brent started the day higher and
stood at one hundred dollars sixty by

19
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.560
mid-morning, while Murban slipped one
dollar thirty to one hundred dollars

20
00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.480
ninety.

21
00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.547
The trigger was the election.

22
00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:03.307
Democrats took both chambers of
Congress, according to Saxo Bank.

23
00:01:03.413 --> 00:01:06.400
Trump told the Financial Times there
were no immediate plans to strike

24
00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.840
Iran, and he put the defeat
down to gasoline prices.

25
00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.933
Vice President Vance went
further, gCaptain reported,

26
00:01:12.987 --> 00:01:15.320
and blamed the eight-month war itself.

27
00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.560
Traders have priced in a settlement,
and that pulled the risk premium

28
00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.813
out of prompt crude.
A deal is only priced,

29
00:01:21.867 --> 00:01:25.960
not agreed. Neither Washington nor
Tehran has published any terms,

30
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.173
and gCaptain argues the defeat
may make an exit harder,

31
00:01:29.227 --> 00:01:32.773
not easier. Gulf flows have
also slipped from recent highs,

32
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.480
and two consultancies, Rystad among
them, warned against counting on

33
00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.200
a quick supply rebound.

34
00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.600
The physical risk is still there.

35
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.480
Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard
Corps says four tankers hit naval

36
00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.027
mines south of Hormuz, in an
area it had declared closed,

37
00:01:48.053 --> 00:01:52.120
and are still burning. It also
says two other vessels were seized.

38
00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.200
That is Iran's claim alone.

39
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.240
No owner, flag state or report from
the UK Maritime Trade Operations

40
00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.840
centre has confirmed it, and anyone
running or chartering tonnage in

41
00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.480
the area will be weighing it all the same.

42
00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.640
Turning to gas. Equinor shut its
Visund platform in the Norwegian North

43
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:12.560
Sea on Wednesday after a fire in
an electrical switchboard room.

44
00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.640
According to NRK, Norway's
public broadcaster,

45
00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.480
all of the field's export capacity
is off the market from Thursday.

46
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.440
That's just over thirteen
million cubic metres a day,

47
00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.760
and no restart date has been reported.

48
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.760
The timing is awkward for European buyers.

49
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.520
EU storage was already drawing, down
about a quarter of a point on the

50
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.280
third of November, according
to Gas Infrastructure Europe.

51
00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.120
Data from the European Centre for
Medium-Range Weather Forecasts also

52
00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.720
show early signs of the
polar vortex breaking down.

53
00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.440
That could send cold air
into Northwest Europe,

54
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.800
though for now it's a
forecast signal, not weather.

55
00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.800
The midterm news did briefly
pull the Dutch TTF contract down,

56
00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:56.240
with the front month off
two percent early Wednesday.

57
00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.160
In Asia, the Japan Korea Marker
topped thirty-one dollars per million

58
00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.400
British thermal units this month.

59
00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.720
It briefly went past thirty-three.

60
00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.760
Back in January it was a little over nine.

61
00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:11.160
Over to US oil products.
According to the EIA,

62
00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.560
distillate stocks fell three point
six million barrels in the week to

63
00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.360
the thirtieth of October.

64
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.653
That leaves them at about ninety-nine
point three million barrels,

65
00:03:19.707 --> 00:03:21.973
the second weekly fall in a row.

66
00:03:22.027 --> 00:03:26.080
And the draw came even as refinery
utilisation rose to ninety-four point

67
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.093
five percent. Higher runs, in other words,

68
00:03:29.147 --> 00:03:31.200
aren't keeping up with offtake.

69
00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.120
Other stocks fell too. Commercial
crude dropped by about nine hundred

70
00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.773
thousand barrels, to just under
four hundred and ten million.

71
00:03:38.827 --> 00:03:41.640
That's four percent below
the five-year average.

72
00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.000
Gasoline slipped by about
two hundred thousand barrels.

73
00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:49.240
Cheaper crude alongside tighter diesel
points to wider distillate cracks,

74
00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.867
which is good news for refiners' margins.

75
00:03:51.893 --> 00:03:55.733
It may also pull more Gulf Coast
barrels toward the US Northeast,

76
00:03:55.787 --> 00:04:00.160
at Europe's expense. Meanwhile, the
American Maritime Partnership is

77
00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.627
urging Trump to let the
emergency Jones Act waiver lapse,

78
00:04:03.653 --> 00:04:05.160
gCaptain reported.

79
00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.960
In petrochemical feedstocks, butane
is at levels not seen in a generation.

80
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.840
Northwest European butane for November
reached eleven hundred and twenty-five

81
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.973
dollars a tonne in early November,
according to OilPrice dot com.

82
00:04:18.027 --> 00:04:23.040
That's the highest in thirty years, and
above the peaks of twenty twenty-two.

83
00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.400
Asia's butane index stood at eleven
hundred and eighty dollars a tonne

84
00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:28.120
on the third of November.

85
00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.680
In the US, Mont Belvieu reached
nine hundred and twenty dollars,

86
00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:36.160
a fourteen-year high. The main driver
is how propane and butane trade

87
00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.240
has been rerouted since
the war began in March.

88
00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:42.800
Cracker operators that run on
liquefied petroleum gas are paying for

89
00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:43.740
it.

90
00:04:43.787 --> 00:04:47.520
Back in the Gulf, the Abu Dhabi
National Oil Company is weighing a third

91
00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.280
crude export pipeline that
would avoid the strait,

92
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:55.120
Bloomberg reported. The UAE already
runs one bypass line and is building

93
00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.880
a second. The report rests on
people familiar with the matter,

94
00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.280
and the company hasn't confirmed it.

95
00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:05.600
Separately, Aramco has started production
from its Zuluf offshore expansion,

96
00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.840
according to Splash twenty-four seven.

97
00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.280
It's designed for up to six
hundred thousand barrels a day.

98
00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.720
The catch is location.
Zuluf sits in the Gulf,

99
00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:18.000
so those barrels still have
to leave through Hormuz.

100
00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.360
A few more things.

101
00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.440
The US Treasury's Office of Foreign
Assets Control on Wednesday sanctioned

102
00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:27.280
a network accused of running fraudulent
ship registries for Iran's shadow

103
00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:32.160
fleet. It also issued an Iran-related
alert and amended a Venezuela-related

104
00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.240
general licence.

105
00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:38.560
CVR Energy will buy two refineries
and a marketing platform from Marathon

106
00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.760
Petroleum, according to
Hydrocarbon Engineering.

107
00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.840
That confirms an unsourced
report from Tuesday.

108
00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.040
Neither the price nor
the sites were named.

109
00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.800
New Jersey is pressing its
ports to refuse Russian diesel.

110
00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:56.840
The tanker Agioi Fanendes is still
tracked toward New York and New Jersey.

111
00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:02.040
And in the UK North Sea, Apache and Wood
workers have walked out on platforms.

112
00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.840
No effect on output has been reported.

113
00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:09.120
What to watch next. EU storage readings
come daily through the eleventh

114
00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:13.360
of November. The Agioi Fanendes is
due in New York and New Jersey on

115
00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:17.880
the seventh. The next EIA weekly
report lands on the eleventh.

116
00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:21.973
And the Jones Act emergency
waiver expires on the fifteenth.

117
00:06:22.027 --> 00:06:25.840
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
